---
// Our Story — folded into the single page (anchor #story).
// FOUNDING STORY DETAILS ARE PLACEHOLDERS — confirm the real story with Mandi House.
---

<section id="story" class="relative z-10 bg-ink px-6 md:px-12 pt-12 md:pt-16 pb-12 md:pb-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-brass/10">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[110rem]">
    <p class="kicker mb-6" data-reveal>[ Our Story ]</p>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
      <div class="md:col-span-7">
        <h2 class="font-display font-light text-cream text-4xl md:text-6xl xl:text-7xl leading-[1.04]" data-reveal>
          Mandi is a Yemeni word for a way of cooking. Meat and rice,
          <span class="text-saffron">slow-smoked together</span> until they
          belong to each other.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-fog leading-relaxed mt-6 max-w-xl" data-reveal>
          Located at 573 Sandringham Road, Sandringham, Auckland, Mandi House is
          a beloved destination for authentic Middle Eastern and South Asian
          cuisine. Known for its signature Mandi dishes, a traditional
          Yemeni-style rice and meat delicacy, the restaurant has carved a name
          for itself among food lovers in Auckland's bustling Sandringham food
          district.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-fog leading-relaxed mt-4 max-w-xl" data-reveal>
          Mandi House offers a casual yet inviting atmosphere, perfect for both
          dine-in and takeaway. The menu features a wide variety of dishes,
          including chicken and lamb mandi, biryanis, kebabs, curries, fried
          rice, and wraps. Their generous portions, affordable pricing, and
          bold, aromatic spices make it a favourite for group meals and family
          feasts. Prices start from around $17.99 for a single serve, with
          family platters also available.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-fog leading-relaxed mt-4 max-w-xl" data-reveal>
          Their standout offering, the whole lamb leg mandi, is especially
          popular for special occasions and weekend feasts. Vegetarians aren't
          left out either, with options like paneer tikka, vegetarian wraps, and
          rice bowls. In addition to the regular menu, Mandi House frequently
          offers weekend specials such as zafrani chicken biryani and lamb paya,
          which attract a loyal following. The friendly service and quick
          turnaround time only add to the appeal.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="md:col-span-5 md:col-start-8 flex flex-col gap-7">
        <div data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker mb-3">[ What we believe ]</p>
          <p class="text-cream text-xl md:text-2xl font-display font-light">
            Generous portions. Honest pricing. Bold, aromatic spice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-t border-brass/15 pt-6" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker mb-3">[ How we cook ]</p>
          <p class="text-fog leading-relaxed">
            Charcoal, time, and overnight marinades. Nothing rushed, nothing cut short.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-t border-brass/15 pt-6" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker mb-3">[ Who it's for ]</p>
          <p class="text-fog leading-relaxed">
            Families, friends and late-night tables who came to share.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- image placeholder — grows to fill the column so both sides end together -->
        <div class="relative flex-1 min-h-[260px] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-brass/15 bg-espresso mt-1" data-reveal>
          <span class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center text-brass/25">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="w-10 h-10" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" />
              <circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5" />
              <path d="M21 15l-5-5L5 21" />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
